<header class="post-header">
<p class="bc-area"><a href="/blog/category/technical-seo/">Technical SEO</a></p>
<h1>Fixing slow pages, starting with the biggest win</h1>
<p class="dek">Slow pages lose readers before they read a word. Where the time usually goes, and what to fix first.</p>
<div class="post-meta">
<address>By <a rel="author" href="/blog/authors/lena-vogt/">Lena Vogt</a>, <span class="person-role">Technical SEO editor</span></address>
<p class="post-date"><time datetime="2026-10-05">5 October 2026</time></p>
</div>
<div class="bc-lead">
<figure class="image">
<picture>
<source type="image/webp" srcset="/blog/media/d9df18e6d7e8625d/320.webp 320w, /blog/media/d9df18e6d7e8625d/480.webp 480w, /blog/media/d9df18e6d7e8625d/640.webp 640w, /blog/media/d9df18e6d7e8625d/800.webp 800w" sizes="(min-width: 56rem) 37rem, calc(100vw - 2rem)">
<img src="/blog/media/d9df18e6d7e8625d/800.png" srcset="/blog/media/d9df18e6d7e8625d/800.png 800w" sizes="(min-width: 56rem) 37rem, calc(100vw - 2rem)" width="800" height="450" alt="A bar chart of page weight by part" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
</picture>
<figcaption>Images weigh the most.</figcaption>
</figure>
